Pharmacy E-commerce Store — Screen Design Brief
Working document for building the store from the 32 curated preview screens (source: theme preview set, 1920 px wide desktop captures). Screens are referenced by the renamed filenames shipped in store_design_screens.zip.
1. Purpose and Overall Flow
This brief explains how each of the 32 screens should be used when building the store: the role every screen plays in the shopper journey, the components it introduces, the patterns worth reusing, responsive behaviour to target, and its dependencies on other screens. The screens come from a pharmacy/wellness theme, so several flows are category-specific — most notably the prescription (Rx) ordering path and medicine subscriptions — and must be built as first-class flows, not afterthoughts.
Primary shopper journey covered by the kit: Discover (01–05 homepage layouts) → Browse & filter catalog (06–09) → Evaluate product (10–11) → Purchase (12–14 cart & checkout, with the Rx path 15–16 branching off checkout) → Manage post-purchase (17–20 account area, 21–22 auth) → Support & content (23–32).
IMPORTANT — Note: five homepage variants exist because the theme sells five layout options. Build exactly ONE homepage for the store (recommended: Layout 1 as the base) and treat the other four as alternate section libraries to borrow modules from. Do not build all five.
2. Global Component and Style System (build once, reuse everywhere)
Nearly every screen is assembled from the same library. Build these shared components first; each per-screen section then only lists what is unique.
